  "question": {
    "text": "Assuming that the degree of hydrolysis is small, the $\\mathrm{pH}$ of $0.1 \\mathrm{M}$ solution of sodium acetate $\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}=1.0 \\times 10^{-5}\\right)$ will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BCHjm",
      "text": "\n$5.0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dBWXa",
      "text": "\n$6.0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "31YYz",
      "text": "\n$8.0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vRPIE",
      "text": "\n$9.0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Sodium acetate is a salt of strong base and weak acid.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\therefore \\mathrm{pH}=7+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{p} K_a+\\frac{1}{2} \\log c \\quad \\text { where } \\\\\n&\\mathrm{p} k_a=-\\log K_a=-\\log 10^{-5}=5 \\\\\n&\\log \\mathrm{c}=\\log 10^{-1}=-1 \\\\\n&\\mathrm{pH}=7+\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}=9.0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
